From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Szczepaniak?= <m.szczepaniak.000@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:39:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gl: rebuild the cached GL context when the app context is
 replaced

gst_gl_base_filter_set_context() only rebuilt filter->context when the
GstGLDisplay changed.  A "gst.gl.app_context" push refreshes
priv->other_context and leaves the now-stale filter->context in place, so
the element keeps rendering into a context the application has replaced.

Rebuild when an already-established other_context is replaced too.  The
guard on the old one being non-NULL keeps ordinary startup out: the first
application context arrives on this same old_display == new_display path,
and rebuilding there calls gl_start() before caps have been negotiated,
which GstGLColorBalance rejects with "Unsupported GstGLTextureTarget
value: 0".

This cannot key on filter->in_caps/out_caps instead, tempting as that is as
a statement of the real precondition: GstGLUploadElement overrides
GstBaseTransform::set_caps without chaining up to GstGLBaseFilter, so its
in_caps/out_caps are always NULL and it would never rebuild - leaving
glupload feeding old-context memory to a glcolorconvert that has moved to
the new one, which fails the buffer with "input memory OpenGL context is
different" and errors out the pipeline.

Needed so glupload/glcolorconvert pick up a rewrapped GstGLContext through
the standard gst_element_set_context() propagation, rather than only on the
next caps change - e.g. after a Qt-based video sink notices the windowing
system silently swapped the underlying native GL context, such as across a
display blank/unblank cycle on SailfishOS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-base/gst-libs/gst/gl/gstglbasefilter.c b/subprojects/gst-plugins-base/gst-libs/gst/gl/gstglbasefilter.c
index cfdb551d79..774d618e3c 100644
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-base/gst-libs/gst/gl/gstglbasefilter.c
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-base/gst-libs/gst/gl/gstglbasefilter.c
@@ -512,9 +512,12 @@ gst_gl_base_filter_set_context (GstElement * element, GstContext * context)
   GstGLBaseFilter *filter = GST_GL_BASE_FILTER (element);
   GstGLBaseFilterClass *filter_class = GST_GL_BASE_FILTER_GET_CLASS (filter);
   GstGLDisplay *old_display, *new_display;
+  GstGLContext *old_other_context;
 
   g_rec_mutex_lock (&filter->priv->context_lock);
   old_display = filter->display ? gst_object_ref (filter->display) : NULL;
+  old_other_context = filter->priv->other_context ?
+      gst_object_ref (filter->priv->other_context) : NULL;
   gst_gl_handle_set_context (element, context, &filter->display,
       &filter->priv->other_context);
   if (filter->display)
@@ -523,7 +526,12 @@ gst_gl_base_filter_set_context (GstElement * element, GstContext * context)
   new_display = filter->display ? gst_object_ref (filter->display) : NULL;
 
   if (old_display && new_display) {
-    if (old_display != new_display) {
+    /* a replaced app context on the same display leaves filter->context stale.
+     * The first one an element receives is not a replacement, and rebuilding
+     * on it would run gl_start() before caps have been negotiated. */
+    if (old_display != new_display
+        || (old_other_context != NULL
+            && old_other_context != filter->priv->other_context)) {
       gst_clear_object (&filter->context);
       if (gst_gl_base_filter_find_gl_context_unlocked (filter)) {
         if (filter->in_caps && filter->out_caps) {
@@ -535,6 +543,7 @@ gst_gl_base_filter_set_context (GstElement * element, GstContext * context)
   g_rec_mutex_unlock (&filter->priv->context_lock);
   gst_clear_object (&old_display);
   gst_clear_object (&new_display);
+  gst_clear_object (&old_other_context);
 
   GST_ELEMENT_CLASS (parent_class)->set_context (element, context);
 }
